---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = 'Affiliate disclosure';
const description = 'How Apostille Atlas may earn money from links to online notarization providers, and which links are affiliate links.';
---
<Base title={title} description={description} updated="2026-11-22">
  <h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1>
  <p><strong>Current status (November 22, 2026):</strong> we have affiliate relationships with Notarize and BlueNotary. Links to those providers may earn us a commission, at no extra cost to you. Every other provider link still goes to that provider's public website, and we earn nothing from it.</p>
  <p>Active affiliate programs:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Notarize, since November 21, 2026</li>
    <li>BlueNotary</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We may apply to affiliate programs run by other providers we cover, such as OneNotary and NotaryLive. If one approves us, links to that provider may become affiliate links, and the provider may pay us a commission at no extra cost to you. We'll list each one here with the date.</p>
  <p>Active affiliate links are marked <span class="aff-tag">affiliate link</span> and carry <code>rel="sponsored"</code>. Other provider links are ordinary links; they are not marked, and we earn nothing from them until a program is listed above.</p>
  <h2>Our rules</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Commissions never change a fee, a fact, or the order of a table.</li>
    <li>If a commission-paying provider is the worse choice for a situation, we say so.</li>
    <li>We include providers that don't pay us whenever leaving them out would make a comparison worse.</li>
    <li>An online notary platform does not issue an apostille. The apostille or authentication certificate comes from the competent authority, usually the secretary of state in the state that issued or notarized the document.</li>
  </ul>
</Base>
